{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Living waters into a vessel.</b> From here is a hint to call up to the Torah a kohen, a levi, and an yisrael — that is: ונתן עליו — the Torah, which is called מים, as it is said: הוי כל צמא לכו למים, and it is also called עץ חיים, as it is said: עץ חיים היא — [אל כלי — in notarikon:] כהן לוי ישראל."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {0 "The notarikon reads the words אל כלי in the verse as an acrostic for כהן לוי ישראל; the parenthetical editorial marker אל כל\"י נוטרי׳ indicates this."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:09:41.118774433Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}